<title>UK: Capital Radio upbeat on radio business.</title>
<headline>Capital Radio upbeat on radio business.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Capital Radio Plc said on Wednesday revenue from its radio business continued to grow at a stronger rate than the overall radio market with its profits for the first quarter &quot;in line with budget&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;We continue to be well placed...&quot; Capital Radio's chairman Ian Irvine told shareholders at its annual general meeting.</p>
<p>Irvine said the Capital Radio Cafe in Leicester Square had made an &quot;encouraging start&quot; since its opening in November.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +0171-542 7717</p>
</text>
